    "## Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "### What This Notebook Contains\n",
    "\n",
    "| Section | Content | Source Notebooks |\n",
    "|:--------|:--------|:-----------------|\n",
    "| 1-3 | Setup, data loading, utilities | All 7 |\n",
    "| 4 | Affine calibrator (trainable calibration layer) | 5, 6, 7 |\n",
    "| 5 | Baseline model definitions (7 models) | 5, 6, 7 |\n",
    "| 6a | XGBoost with custom contrastive objective | 1, 2 |\n",
    "| 6b | RandomForest with contrastive calibration | 1, 2 |\n",
    "| 7 | Mixture of Experts (two-expert MoE) | 3, 4 |\n",
    "| 8 | Multi-baselines with affine calibration | 5, 6 |\n",
    "| 9 | Mix-weight sweep | 7 |\n",
    "| 10-11 | Execution and results saving | All |\n",
    "| 12-13 | Visualization | All |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Design Decisions\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Affine calibration layer**: For non-differentiable models (RF, SVR, etc.),\n",
    "   contrastive learning is applied via a post-hoc calibration layer rather than\n",
    "   modifying the base model's objective.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **Subsampling for CL normalization**: The contrastive loss normalization\n",
    "   constant (cl0) is estimated via mini-batch subsampling to avoid O(n^2)\n",
    "   memory usage.\n",
    "\n",
    "3. **Consistent evaluation**: All models use the same Random(70/15/15) and\n",
    "   GroupSplit(grid_id) splits, and report All/Tail/Worst-case metrics.\n",
    "\n",
    "4. **From original notebooks 1-2**: XGBoost with custom CL objective and\n",
    "   RandomForest with calibration head.\n",
    "\n",
    "5. **From original notebooks 3-4**: MoE with body/tail experts and gating,\n",
    "   using signed_log1p transformation for the tail expert.\n",
    "\n",
    "6. **From original notebooks 5-7**: Multi-baseline comparison with affine\n",
    "   calibration and weight sweep experiments."
   ]
